{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the acute angle formed by the hour hand and the minute hand of a clock at 3:20, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the position of the minute hand.\n2. Calculate the position of the hour hand.\n3. Determine the difference in their positions.\n4. Convert the difference into degrees.\n5. Ensure the angle is acute (i.e., less than 180 degrees).\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the position of the minute hand.**\n\nThe minute hand moves 360 degrees in 60 minutes. Therefore, it moves 6 degrees per minute.\nAt 20 minutes past the hour, the minute hand is at:\n\\[ 20 \\times 6 = 120 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nThis is measured from the 12 o'clock position.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the position of the hour hand.**\n\n","prefix_end":705,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,29783,9210,14122,553,279,6460,1424,323,279,9383,1424,315,264,8866,518,220,18,25,17,15,11,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,20517,279,2309,315,279,9383,1424,624,17,13,20517,279,2309,315,279,6460,1424,624,18,13,29901,279,6672,304,862,9892,624,19,13,7169,279,6672,1119,12348,624,20,13,29279,279,9210,374,29783,320,72,1734,2572,2686,1091,220,16,23,15,12348,3593,334,8304,220,16,25,20517,279,2309,315,279,9383,1424,13,56177,785,9383,1424,10797,220,18,21,15,12348,304,220,21,15,4420,13,15277,11,432,10797,220,21,12348,817,9383,624,1655,220,17,15,4420,3267,279,6460,11,279,9383,1424,374,518,510,78045,220,17,15,1124,15136,220,21,284,220,16,17,15,1124,1318,90,12348,92,1124,921,1986,374,16878,504,279,220,16,17,297,62410,2309,382,334,8304,220,17,25,20517,279,2309,315,279,6460,1424,13,56177,785,6460,1424,10797,220,18,21,15,12348,304,220,16,17,4115,11,773,432,10797,220,18,15,12348,817,6460,13,22406,11,432,10797,220,15,13,20,12348,817,9383,320,11284,17767,18,15,1124,1318,90,12348,7530,413,92,1124,611,220,21,15,1124,1318,90,4420,7530,413,92,284,220,1