26,-0.1363002210855484,-1.728519782773219e-05,-0.0002004899288294837,-0.2715230882167816,-0.9099308848381042,-5.960462772236497e-07,-0.6535918712615967,-0.9988604187965393,0.0,0.0,-0.011317813768982887,-0.00015484087634831667,-1.5497195136049413e-06,0.0,-1.2636104656849056e-05,-0.21330209076404572,-1.9899107217788696,-0.005808379966765642,-0.000163541772053577,-0.019220300018787384,-0.8892862200737,-0.000597179401665926,-7.152555099310121e-07,0.0,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,-1.7881377516459906e-06,-2.264974000354414e-06,-3.6954811548639555e-06,-2.658331868587993e-05],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,1655,220,18,25,17,15,11,1128,374,279,8381,6629,315,279,29783,9210,14122,553,279,6460,1424,323,279,9383,1424,389,264,220,16,17,21231,23400,8866,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nAt 3:20, what is the degree measure of the acute angle formed by the hour hand and the minute hand on a 12-hour analog clock?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"d2e99364f168fa81c5beb53455d3225f99bfef6b26d25d8eb860a85781eca74b"},"seconds":12.31378722190857,"seed":285424713028099395,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the acute angle formed by the hour hand and the minute hand of a clock at 3:20, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the position of the minute hand.\n2. Calculate the position of the hour hand.\n3. Determine the difference in their positions.\n4. Convert the difference into degrees.\n5. Ensure the angle is acute (i.e., less than 180 degrees).\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the position of the minute hand.**\n\nThe minute hand moves 360 degrees in 60 minutes. Therefore, it moves 6 degrees per minute.\nAt 20 minutes past the hour, the minute hand is at:\n\\[ 20 \\times 6 = 120 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nThis is measured from the 12 o'clock position.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the position of the hour hand.**\n\nThe hour hand moves 360 degrees in 12 hours, so it moves 30 degrees per hour. Additionally, it moves 0.5 degrees per minute (since \\(30 \\text{ degrees/hour} \\div 60 \\text{ minutes/hour} = 0.5 \\text{ degrees/minute}\\)).\n\nAt 3:00, the hour hand is at:\n\\[ 3 \\times 30 = 90 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nBy 3:20, the hour hand has moved an additional:\n\\[ 20 \\times 0.5 = 10 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nSo, at 3:20, the hour hand is at:\n\\[ 90 + 10 = 100 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nThis is measured from the 12 o'clock position.\n\n**Step 3: Determine the difference in their positions.**\n\nThe difference between the positions of the hour hand and the minute hand is:\n\\[ 120 - 100 = 20 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nor\n\\[ 360 - 120 + 100 = 240 \\text{ degrees} \\]\nSince we are asked for the acute angle, we take the smaller of the two differences, which is 20 degrees.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{20}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:721"}
